<title>CHINA: HSBC shares hit high on warrants talk.</title>
<headline>HSBC shares hit high on warrants talk.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of HSBC Holdings Plc rose on market talk that a merchant bank was planning a covered warrant issue on the bank, brokers said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The issuer accumulating shares to cover the warrant and some follow-through overseas buying aided the rise of the stock,&quot; said a sales manager at a regional brokerage.</p>
<p>Brokers said investors may also be starting to accumulate the stock on hopes of strong earnings ahead of the release of the bank's interim results due on August 4.</p>
<p>HSBC shares were up HK$4.00 to HK$245 in late trade after touching a new high of HK$247.</p>
<p>Volume was 4.18 million shares worth HK$1.02 billion.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
